WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.450
- You said your mom, this
is actually adorable.

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.640
You said your mom ordered
a song from heaven.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:05.592
- Oh god, yeah.

00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:06.425
- Please explain.

00:00:06.425 --> 00:00:08.710
- Oh man, so I have a song on
my record called "She'd Say."

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:11.690
And basically it's been 10
years since I lost my mom.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:13.797
And I walked into my house
this year and my wife goes,

00:00:13.797 --> 00:00:16.810
"Oh, I got you a phone call
with a medium today at 1 p.m."

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.380
And I was like, "Uh, okay."

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.260
I feel like I'm supposed to
pretend like I'm against that.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:21.582
I'm like, kind of into that.

00:00:21.582 --> 00:00:22.415
So--

00:00:22.415 --> 00:00:23.409
- Yeah, oh I'm into all
of that stuff, yeah.

00:00:23.409 --> 00:00:26.957
- So I make the call and
the guy immediately goes,

00:00:26.957 --> 00:00:27.790
"Oh yeah, your mom's here.

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:28.760
"Cathy right?"

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:30.157
I'm like, "Sure."
- What?

00:00:30.157 --> 00:00:31.222
- "Okay, keep going."

00:00:31.222 --> 00:00:32.060
- He could have Googled.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:32.910
- He could have Googled.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.727
And he goes, "She really wants you,

00:00:34.727 --> 00:00:35.737
"she's like, very adamant.

00:00:35.737 --> 00:00:39.207
"She need you to write a song
from her to your daughter

00:00:39.207 --> 00:00:41.109
"about everything she would
say to her if she was there,

00:00:41.109 --> 00:00:42.310
"because she can't be there to say it."

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:43.980
- [Kelly] Are you trying to make me cry?

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.150
- I know, it was rough.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.930
So I'm like, "Oh my god,
that's such a good idea."

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:50.370
And I'm like, "That's a good idea."

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:52.160
And then I write the song.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.620
And my mom loved
"Graceland" by Paul Simon.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:55.453
- Yeah.

00:00:55.453 --> 00:00:57.290
- So I get this phone call
where she orders the song.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.290
Apparently.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:59.220
I write the song.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.090
And then I get in the
car and turn on the radio

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:03.700
and on the radio's like,
"Ladysmith Black Mambazo,"

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.880
which is the group that he
went to make "Graceland" with.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.560
They're nine males from South Africa.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:11.550
They're like, "They're gonna
be in Los Angeles on Friday."

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:14.080
And I was like, sitting
in the car like, "What?"

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:14.913
- What, yeah!

00:01:14.913 --> 00:01:16.900
- The hell is going on!

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:20.860
So we chased them down and
they came into the studio

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:23.437
and they surrounded me and
they're singing in Zulu

00:01:23.437 --> 00:01:26.670
"I miss my mom and that's
what she'd say," in Zulu.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.010
And we like wrote this
song for my little girl.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:30.690
And at the end you can
hear my little girl's voice

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.062
say like, "Grandma Cathy" on it.

00:01:32.062 --> 00:01:33.520
- Oh no!

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:35.500
It's like you're just trying to kill me.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:39.480
- And what's nuts is now that
insane experience for me,

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:40.480
a lot of people have heard it

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.050
in different parts of their lives

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:44.220
and been like "Oh, that's my grandma,"

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.880
or "That's my mother
that I lost," you know.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:46.713
It's been wild.

00:01:46.713 --> 00:01:47.546
- That is incredible.

00:01:47.546 --> 00:01:49.300
'Cause at first were you very skeptic?

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:51.045
You were like, "Okay, you Googled my mom."

00:01:51.045 --> 00:01:52.490
- I was a little bit skeptical,

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:55.720
but that idea is very her, so yeah.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:56.610
- Wow!

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:57.443
What a power, and then--

00:01:57.443 --> 00:01:59.840
- So I think if you've lost anyone,

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.930
I'm pretty sure they see everything.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:03.560
- Yeah, so watch what you're doing!

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:04.630
- Honestly.

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:06.530
And then I also think that
they can just like order songs.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:10.420
So, those are both things.
- Oh my gosh, I love you!

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:12.673
They're just like ordering
songs from heaven.

